<%# The "Eigene Konfiguration" pane (doc/ki_zugang_umbau_plan.md D6/D8).

    Until this rebuild the same content was a CARD below the package grid — the one entry
    in a list that was not a member of it (P2 of the plan). It is an alternative way, so
    it is now a pane of its own, shown instead of the grid rather than under it.

    ORDER is the instruction it should read as: what is on record, then the door to
    setting it up, then taking this way. Nothing here decides anything about jurisdiction
    — whatever the organisation configures behind that door is what applies, which is
    also why this way was never filterable. %>
<%# TWO questions, and conflating them is what made the page lie (D7):
      custom_selected — is this the way in force? (blank package id, convention E1-C)
      configured      — is anything actually behind it? (own credentials on record)
    "Gewählt" needs both. A fresh organisation satisfies only the first, and used to read
    "Eigene Konfiguration · Gewählt" for a decision nobody had made. %>
<% custom_selected = @organisation.ai_package_id.blank? %>
<% configured = @organisation.ai_custom_access_configured? %>
<div class="mt-6 rounded-lg border border-cream-300 bg-cream-50 p-5" id="ai_package_custom">
  <% if custom_selected && configured %>
    <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded border border-ink bg-ink px-2 py-1 text-xs font-bold text-cream-50">
      <i class="bi bi-check-lg mr-1"></i><%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.custom.selected_badge') %>
    </span>
  <% end %>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-cream-800"><%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.custom.description') %></p>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-cream-800"><%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.custom.note') %></p>

  <%# The door §3.4 asked for from the start: "Vor der Einrichtung ist das eine
      Navigationszeile („Einrichten →"), nach der Einrichtung eine vollwertige Option
      mit Statuszeile." Until S7 the card was the WAHL with nothing behind it — the
      EINRICHTUNG was a form further down the same page, which is how this page came to
      ask one question twice (E6). The link is here whether or not this way is in force:
      preparing an access before switching to it is the natural order, and it is the
      order the connection test follows since L6 was closed. %>
  <div class="mt-4 border-t border-cream-300 pt-4">
    <% if configured %>
      <p class="mb-2 text-sm text-cream-700">
        <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.custom.access_present',
              provider: @organisation.ai_provider_display_name) %>
        <% if @organisation.ai_connection_failed? %>
          <span class="font-bold text-red-700">
            <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle mr-1"></i><%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.custom.access_failed') %>
          </span>
        <% end %>
      </p>
    <% else %>
      <%# Absence, stated. It was silence before: the line only appeared once credentials
          existed, so the pane said nothing at all in the state where there is most to
          say. %>
      <p class="mb-2 text-sm text-cream-700">
        <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.custom.not_configured') %>
      </p>
      <% if custom_selected %>
        <%# Z3 in full: this way is in force AND nothing is behind it, so no AI call can
            succeed. No new bar on the button that got the org here — the way back stays
            clickable exactly as before (D7); the pane just stops pretending. %>
        <p class="mb-2 text-sm text-amber-800">
          <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle mr-1.5"></i>
          <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.custom.not_ready_hint') %>
        </p>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
    <%= link_to organisation_ai_configuration_path(@organisation),
          class: 'inline-flex items-center text-sm font-bold text-cream-900 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-ink' do %>
      <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.custom.configure_link') %>
      <i class="bi bi-arrow-right ml-1.5"></i>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <% unless custom_selected %>
    <div class="mt-5">
      <%# The way BACK, and it asks the SAME question the package cards ask
          (@custom_switch_blocked ← Factory.embedding_switch?, package: nil):
          leaving a package moves the embedding lane in exactly the cases
          joining one does (Falle 5), so it is one rule, not two.
          And it takes the same detour as the card door since P4b: the way back
          re-embeds just as much corpus as the way in, so it goes through the
          consequence dialog too. Blank id = "Eigene Konfiguration" there as
          well (E1-C), which is why the link carries no ai_package_id. %>
      <% if @custom_switch_blocked %>
        <p class="text-sm text-cream-800 mb-3"><%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.custom.switch_notice') %></p>
        <%= render Neo::Buttons::ButtonComponent.new(
          variant: :secondary,
          size: :medium,
          icon: "arrow-left-right",
          url: confirm_package_organisation_ai_settings_path(
            @organisation, package_mode: Organisations::AiSettingsController::MODE_CUSTOM
          )
        ) do %>
          <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.card.switch_button') %>
        <% end %>
      <% else %>
        <%# Same Actor, blank id — deselecting is one write, not a second code path. %>
        <%= render Neo::Buttons::ButtonComponent.new(
          variant: :secondary,
          size: :medium,
          form: { action: select_package_organisation_ai_settings_path(@organisation),
                  method: :post,
                  params: { ai_package_id: '' } }
        ) do %>
          <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.custom.select_button') %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
